## 2. Grading Round-A Proposals by Theoretical Spine

- **Mathematically Flawed — [A4_wildcard.md](file:///Users/neo/repos/polyformer/research/meta/chew/A4_wildcard.md#L50-L65) Survivor B ("Nerode census of speech, birdsong, whale codas"):**
  - Estimating stochastic Nerode classes from sequence distributions is already **computational mechanics** (**Shalizi & Crutchfield, 2001, *J. Stat. Phys.* 104:817–879 / arXiv:cond-mat/9907176** — defined **causal states**, the probabilistic Myhill–Nerode classes of a stochastic process, and their **$\epsilon$-machine** complexity). Worse, for any continuous neural LM or power-law process (**Sainburg, Theilman, Thielk & Gentner, 2019, *Nat. Commun.* 10:5036** — showed both birdsong and speech exhibit power-law mutual information decay), exact future distributions never collide ($N(d) = |\Sigma|^d$); under an $\epsilon$-clustering tolerance, $N_\epsilon(d)$ merely re-measures mutual information decay, not a Chomsky-hierarchy boundary.
- **Empirical Only (No Predictive Theorem) — [A2_language.md](file:///Users/neo/repos/polyformer/research/meta/chew/A2_language.md#L31) #2 (Indirect poverty-of-stimulus), [A1_nature_anatomy.md](file:///Users/neo/repos/polyformer/research/meta/chew/A1_nature_anatomy.md#L48) #3 (Self-training counterexamples), [A4_wildcard.md](file:///Users/neo/repos/polyformer/research/meta/chew/A4_wildcard.md#L66) Survivor C (Lean arXiv audit):**
  - Our whiteboard §5 ([OVERNIGHT_2026-10-28.md](file:///Users/neo/repos/polyformer/research/OVERNIGHT_2026-10-28.md#L371)) refuted our finite-teaching-set conjecture beyond **Goldman & Kearns (1995, *J. Comput. Syst. Sci.* 50:20–31)** (defined teaching dimension for deterministic concepts).

